<%# The first-share moment. Shows once, when a student holds something and has not dismissed it.

    Inline rather than a modal: on a shared Chromebook a modal gets dismissed by whoever walks
    past, and this is the one message worth not missing. It also cannot cover the page it is
    explaining.

    It explains *owning*, not buying - "you own part of a company" is the concept shift, and it
    says nothing about whether the purchase was clever. The copy says "you hold", never "you just
    bought", so it is accurate for any holder, which matters because nothing was backfilled.

    On components/ui/_callout with the :info tone rather than a hand-rolled panel. It was
    bg-teal-50 / border-teal-200 / text-teal-900 - Tailwind's teal, which is a mint green and not
    this product's brand: sitf-primary is #00698c, a blue-teal. An informational panel is blue in
    every system that ships one, and the callout's blue is measured. A bespoke panel was also how
    the mint got in: the component was built two commits earlier and then not used here. %>
<% return unless current_user.student? && @portfolio.celebrate_first_share? %>

<%= render layout: "components/ui/callout",
           locals: { tone: :info,
                     icon: "chart-pie",
                     title: "You own part of a company",
                     body: "You hold #{pluralize(@insights.company_count, 'company')}. That makes you one of its owners - when the company is worth more, your shares are worth more too.",
                     testid: "first-share" } do %>
  <%# button_to renders its own form, which is fine here: this sits between cards, never inside
      another form. %>
  <%= button_to acknowledge_first_share_portfolio_path(@portfolio),
                method: :patch,
                class: ghost_class do %>
    <%= lucide_icon "x", class: "size-4 shrink-0" %>
    Dismiss
  <% end %>
<% end %>
